  "body": "From https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/1679\n\n> The `rp` check only works for direct children of `rp`, not descendants (e.g. `<ruby><rp><span>(</span></rp>...`). Do we want that to work? Or change the content model or `rp` to \"text\"?\n\nI think we should change the content model of `pr` to \"text\". I see no use case to allow anything else in it, and allowing markup either complicates `innerText` or gives weird results.\n\ncc @sideshowbarker \n",
